# Line endings are part of the repository's contract: every text file is stored with LF and checked out with LF on
# every OS, whatever core.autocrlf says, so a checkout is byte-identical on Windows, macOS and Linux. Tests compare
# files byte for byte (a generated document against its rendering, a copy against its source) and never normalise
# line endings. No checked-in file needs CRLF (the CSV the extension writes has CRLF records, made by code, not
# stored here). A file that ever must be CRLF is listed below with `eol=crlf` and the reason.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never converted, never diffed as text.
*.wav binary
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.tgz binary
*.whl binary
*.vsix binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.wasm binary
*.npy binary
*.npz binary

# The GUI core is a byte-for-byte copy of the wandas-gui repository, held to pinned hashes (scripts/sync-gui-core.mjs
# checks them): git keeps these bytes exactly as committed (LF, as upstream) and never converts them.
src/shared/gui-core/** -text
scripts/sync-gui-core.mjs -text
